      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.1 Internet"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Internet is a global network of interconnected computers using the TCP/IP protocol suite.",
        "The World Wide Web (WWW) is a system of interlinked hypertext documents accessed via web browsers.",
        "Web Browsers retrieve and display web pages, while Search Engines index and locate online content.",
        "Email relies on protocols such as SMTP for sending messages, and POP3 or IMAP for receiving them.",
        "URLs uniquely identify web resources, and HTTPS ensures encrypted and secure web data transfer."
      ],
      "id": "vcrrfrg"
