    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "BCC (Blind Carbon Copy) hides recipient email addresses from other recipients, whereas CC (Carbon Copy) keeps them visible.",
        "HTTP operates over default Port 80, whereas secure HTTPS operates over Port 443.",
        "Tim Berners-Lee created the World Wide Web (WWW) at CERN in 1989.",
        "SMTP is exclusively used for sending emails, while POP3/IMAP protocols are used to fetch/retrieve emails."
      ],
      "id": "awye71l"
